# Unified Messenger — agent rules

**The working agreement for this repository is [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md). Read it before doing anything
else.** It carries the hard constraints, the build and publish sequence, and a table of gotchas that were
each learned by getting them wrong once. Do not re-derive the facts recorded there.

This file exists because Cursor reads it and cannot follow an include. Everything below is a summary; where
it and `AGENTS.md` differ, `AGENTS.md` is right.

> **This file used to describe a different product.** Until v4.99.53 it described the v1 idea — "multiple
> instances of web-based social media platforms" whose "defining feature is a unified native Notification
> Tab" — and told agents to search the web before proposing anything. None of that survived contact with
> what this became. It also said *instances*, the word the product deliberately stopped using and that
> `AccountVocabularyTests` now fails the build over. Two documents disagreeing about what the product is
> costs more than one missing document, so this is a pointer now rather than a second opinion.

## What this is

A **free, fully-local Windows oversight app** for a multi-location business owner. It passively watches
customer conversations (WhatsApp first) plus Google Business **reviews**, and surfaces who is still waiting
for a reply: on-time %, awaiting counts, stale accounts, a worst-first command centre.

It is an **oversight tool**, not a messaging client. It never sends.

## Hard constraints — a change that breaks one is not a fix

1. Nothing on cloud. No APIs. No recurring cost.
2. **Zero oversight data leaves the machine** — no telemetry, analytics or crash upload, ever. This governs
   data the app derives. A browse tab the owner opens is their own traffic, on a separate WebView2 profile;
   oversight data must never reach it.
3. The app never auto-sends. Read-only scraping only.
4. All AI is on-device via Ollama.
5. No unofficial protocol libraries (Baileys, whatsmeow, …) — ban risk. Readable for DOM knowledge, never
   vendored. GPL/AGPL sources are reference-only.
6. Google is **reviews and Q&A only, permanently** — Google Business Messages was shut down in July 2024
   and the data deleted. Do not add awaiting-reply or message-count plumbing for it.
7. Never write scraped payloads, customer names or message text into `app.log`. Log lengths and types.
   That file is what support asks the owner to send.

## Vocabulary

The product's word is **account**. "Instance" is a type name and must not appear in any user-visible string
or accessible name — `AccountVocabularyTests` fails the build on it. The one allowed phrase is "Ollama
instance".

## Stack

WinUI 3 / Windows App SDK, .NET 8, unpackaged (`WindowsPackageType=None`), WebView2 per account,
CommunityToolkit.Mvvm, OllamaSharp, xUnit, Inno Setup.

## Before you push

Run the **full** test suite — `dotnet test UnifiedMessenger.Tests/UnifiedMessenger.Tests.csproj -c Release`.
Kill any running `UnifiedMessenger.exe` first, or the single-instance pipe tests fail for reasons that look
like code breakage. Filters are for iteration only; they have hidden red tests across several pushes before.
